<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61970" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάρῑσα</span></b>  [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾱρ],
		ἡ</span> (not <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λάρισσα</span>, v.
		<i><span class="en">
			Arc.
			77.14
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			<u>IG</u>
			9(2).60.5
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			525.5
		</span></i>, al., but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαρισσέοις</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
			9(2).6c3
		</span></i>), <u>Larissa</u>, a name of many old Greek cities, <i><span class="en">
			Il.
			2.841
		</span></i>, etc.; Pelasgic acc. to <i><span class="en">
			Str.
			9.5.19
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			13.3.2
		</span></i>: an 
			Ion.
		 form <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λήρισαι</span> (in Aeolis)
		occurs in <i><span class="en">
			Hdt.
			1.149
		</span></i>; orig. it denoted a <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>citadel</i>, such as <i>the Larissa</i> of Argos, <i><span class="en">
				St.Byz.
			</span></i>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				1.40
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			Adj.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λᾱρῑσαῖος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
				<i>Larissaean, of</i> or <i>from Larissa</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Th.
				2.22
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>HG</u>
				3.1.7
			</span></i>, etc.; 
				Ion.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ληρις</span></b> - <i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				9.1
			</span></i> and <i><span class="en">
				58
			</span></i>:—also <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαρίσιος</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λαρισηνός</span></b>  as epith. of Zeus, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				9.5.19
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.3.2
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Λᾱρῑσαῖοι</span></b> 
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἑ&lt;&gt;ητῆρες</span>
			<u>Larissaean</u> pots for boiling, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				6.305
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Leon.
			</span></i>); <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λᾱρῑσοποιοί</span></b>  for
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λαρισαιοποιοί</span>, either
				<i>makers of Larissaean pots</i>, or <i>makers of Larissaean
				citizens</i>, of the <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δημιουργοί</span> (magistrates), <i><span class="en">
				Gorg.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1275b30
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
